🧭 Phase 0 — Foundation (you’re basically here)

Goal: Prove you can run a timed, structured data pipeline.

Work:

Non-blocking loop with millis()
CSV-style output
IMUSample struct
Simulated data (trend + oscillation + noise)

Done when:

Output is stable, well-formatted, and repeatable
🧪 Phase 1 — Data Realism & Hygiene (1–2 days)

Goal: Make your fake data look like a real sensor and clean your pipeline.

Work:

Tune ranges (ay ~ [-2, 2], az ~ 9.8 ± small noise)
Fix ring buffer (write at tail, wrap correctly, don’t advance head unless reading)
Add CSV header once in setup()
Pick a reasonable sample rate (e.g., 100–200 ms for now)

Done when:

ax = trend, ay = oscillation, az = small random noise
Buffer logic is correct and simple
🔌 Phase 2 — IMU Bring-Up (2–3 days)

Goal: Replace fake data with real MPU-6050 data.

Work:

Wire IMU (I2C)
Read raw ax, ay, az, gx, gy, gz
Print raw values in CSV (no filtering yet)
Verify axes change as you move the board

Done when:

You can tilt/move the sensor and see sensible changes
Data is clearly noisy/drifty
🔍 Phase 3 — Understand Raw Data (1–2 days)

Goal: Build intuition about what’s wrong with real data.

Work:

Observe noise (still sensor)
Observe drift (gyro over time)
Observe spikes (taps/impacts)
Compare to your simulated data

Done when:

You can point to: noise, drift, spikes in your logs
🧹 Phase 4 — Basic Filtering (2–3 days)

Goal: Make data usable.

Work:

Moving average (use your ring buffer)
Simple low-pass behavior (smooth vs lag tradeoff)
Compare raw vs filtered side-by-side

Done when:

Noise visibly reduced
You can explain the tradeoff (smoothness vs responsiveness)
🧠 Phase 5 — Derived Signals (2–3 days)

Goal: Turn raw data into meaningful quantities.

Work:

Compute tilt (pitch/roll) from accelerometer (conceptually)
Integrate gyro short-term (see drift)
Combine ideas (even a simple complementary-style blend, conceptually)

Done when:

You output a stable angle estimate that reacts to motion
⚠️ Phase 6 — Fault Handling (1–2 days)

Goal: Make your system robust.

Work:

Detect spikes (thresholds vs recent history)
Handle missing/late samples (timing checks)
Sanity checks (impossible values)

Done when:

System flags/ignores bad data instead of trusting everything
💾 Phase 7 — Data Logging (2 days)

Goal: Persist data for analysis.

Work:

Write CSV to microSD
Log: time, raw, filtered, derived values
Organize runs (one file per test)

Done when:

You can remove the SD card and open clean datasets on your PC
🚗 Phase 8 — Real-World Testing (2–4 days)

Goal: Validate under motion.

Work:

Mount on RC car (or simple moving platform)
Run controlled tests:
straight acceleration
stops
turns
Compare expectations vs logs

Done when:

You can explain what each maneuver looks like in data
📊 Phase 9 — Analysis & Presentation (2–3 days)

Goal: Turn work into a strong project.

Work:

Plot data (optional but powerful)
Quantify improvements (before/after filtering)
Write clear README:
architecture
constraints (timing, memory)
results (with examples)

Done when:

Someone can understand your system in 2–3 minutes
🗓️ Suggested 4–5 Week Timeline
Week 1: Phases 0–2 (you’re nearly through)
Week 2: Phases 3–4
Week 3: Phases 5–6
Week 4: Phases 7–8
Week 5 (optional): Phase 9 polish
